Anyway, those were the tough days, but they taught me resilience, or maybe I was born with it.

2505
02:26:00,960 --> 02:26:03,995
One difference between us, meaning between her and I,

2506
02:26:04,075 --> 02:26:07,190
is that I managed to get a good university education,

2507
02:26:07,270 --> 02:26:10,820
and at twenty I had the chance to go to the US for a semester.

2508
02:26:10,900 --> 02:26:11,900
Now you think about it.

2509
02:26:12,100 --> 02:26:14,130
A girl from Garden Rancho Land shoe market,

2510
02:26:14,210 --> 02:26:18,466
who was spending her 16th birthday by increasing her tuition, and in McDonald's,

2511
02:26:18,546 --> 02:26:19,600
she spent one year's night.

2512
02:26:19,680 --> 02:26:23,600
The same girl from the night shift, at the age of 20, was studying in America.

2513
02:26:23,680 --> 02:26:29,600
Right? So the world of the perpetrator is different, the world of the complainer is different.

2514
02:26:29,680 --> 02:26:33,600
Regardless of what background they have. Okay?

2515
02:26:33,680 --> 02:26:38,600
She went for the USA semester and now I am doing my masters in Norway.

2516
02:26:38,680 --> 02:26:40,600
But the biggest difference is I am a woman.

2517
02:26:40,680 --> 02:26:45,640
Being a woman and dreaming in Karachi and fulfilling them is a different challenge.

2518
02:26:45,720 --> 02:26:47,261
It was a different challenge.

2519
02:26:47,341 --> 02:26:52,285
When people used to say, don't fly too much, don't fly too much, I still remember that.

2520
02:26:52,365 --> 02:26:55,439
And even today, sometimes those voices echo in my mind.

2521
02:26:55,519 --> 02:26:57,755
But thank God I left all of them behind.

2522
02:26:57,835 --> 02:27:05,950
One of the things I admire about you is how you've managed to build a strong circle of friends who support you and share your vision.

2523
02:27:06,030 --> 02:27:08,123
I don't know which friends are mine.

2524
02:27:08,203 --> 02:27:09,768
Where do you see my friends?

2525
02:27:09,848 --> 02:27:10,495
A little bit.

2526
02:27:10,575 --> 02:27:11,820
I've made some good friends.

2527
02:27:11,900 --> 02:27:18,740
from Karachi too and they are kind people with good hearts but there is one major issue they lack drive.

2528
02:27:18,820 --> 02:27:20,820
That's why they are in Karachi.

2529
02:27:20,900 --> 02:27:21,791
Let's come to this.

2530
02:27:21,871 --> 02:27:28,059
They seem content to just breeze through life without the hunger to push harder to want more and it's such a turn off.

2531
02:27:28,139 --> 02:27:33,970
I see my friends back home stuck in their comfort zones with no ambition to take risks or challenge themselves.

2532
02:27:34,050 --> 02:27:37,400
It's disheartening especially when they are in the comfort zone.

2533
02:27:39,430 --> 02:27:43,950
Especially when you've spent years working so hard to escape that very mindset.

2534
02:27:44,030 --> 02:27:47,110
Yes, I've made some amazing friends here in Norway.

2535
02:27:47,190 --> 02:27:50,530
Many of them are white and have been incredibly welcoming.

2536
02:27:50,610 --> 02:27:54,350
But no matter how great they are, this is still a super white country.

2537
02:27:54,430 --> 02:27:58,290
It gets very lonely and I find myself craving the warmth of home.

2538
02:27:58,370 --> 02:28:00,310
By home, I don't just mean the place.

2539
02:28:00,390 --> 02:28:02,710
I don't miss Karachi for sure.

2540
02:28:02,790 --> 02:28:06,230
But the people who understand the struggles, the grind, the shared.

2541
02:28:06,310 --> 02:28:09,865
shared jokes in Urdu and the sense of community.

2542
02:28:09,945 --> 02:28:16,375
As an avid reader of Urdu literature and poetry and the founder of several book clubs back home,

2543
02:28:16,455 --> 02:28:17,646
I am parched here.

2544
02:28:17,726 --> 02:28:21,364
I want to find like-minded, hard-working, desi friends,

2545
02:28:21,444 --> 02:28:25,029
people with the same fire in their belly that I feel.

2546
02:28:25,109 --> 02:28:27,755
Unfortunately, I have found none so far.

2547
02:28:27,835 --> 02:28:34,190
Here, I often sit and think, Junaid Bhai, you have made those connections in your life.

2548
02:28:34,270 --> 02:28:36,093
How to make connections.

2549
02:28:36,173 --> 02:28:39,707
Have you ever felt this loneliness?

2550
02:28:39,787 --> 02:28:43,990
Did you ever feel that it is not on your wavelength?

2551
02:28:44,070 --> 02:28:47,390
I am working very hard here, I have come a long way,

2552
02:28:47,470 --> 02:28:52,534
but sometimes I feel so lonely that it seems that even after achieving all this,

2553
02:28:52,614 --> 02:28:54,990
a part of my heart remains empty.

2554
02:28:55,070 --> 02:29:01,340
If you have any advice, any words of wisdom for me, then please share it. Maybe it will help you.

2555
02:29:01,420 --> 02:29:03,540
I hope I can get some satisfaction from listening to you.

2556
02:29:03,620 --> 02:29:05,820
So, you saw the email.

2557
02:29:05,900 --> 02:29:09,380
First of all, congratulations. You've made it out of that.

2558
02:29:09,460 --> 02:29:12,940
Whatever came out of that neighborhood has been successful in life.

2559
02:29:13,020 --> 02:29:17,500
Because he saw that, man, these are my circumstances today.

2560
02:29:17,580 --> 02:29:18,780
This cannot be my whole life.

2561
02:29:18,860 --> 02:29:23,807
So all the people who came out of there, first of all, my neighbor,

2562
02:29:23,887 --> 02:29:26,620
who is now a billionaire, man.

2563
02:29:26,700 --> 02:29:28,750
He called, I told you last week.

2564
02:29:28,830 --> 02:29:29,616
He called me.

2565
02:29:29,696 --> 02:29:30,616
It was so nice.

2566
02:29:30,696 --> 02:29:34,144
So yeah, there are so many examples.

2567
02:29:34,224 --> 02:29:36,290
Some in Canada, some in Canada.

2568
02:29:36,370 --> 02:29:39,715
Some country manager of a pharmaceutical company.

2569
02:29:39,795 --> 02:29:42,267
Yeah man, wonderful examples.

2570
02:29:42,347 --> 02:29:46,691
I think when you push so so hard in life, life is like a spring,

2571
02:29:46,771 --> 02:29:49,170
you push forward as much as you can.

2572
02:29:49,250 --> 02:29:53,528
Your desire increases so much that you want to get out of here.

2573
02:29:53,608 --> 02:29:54,741
You get fired up.

2574
02:29:54,821 --> 02:29:55,700
So I think also

2575
02:29:55,780 --> 02:30:02,437
The thing about that neighborhood is that they are very stubborn and the kind of stubborn people there are,

2576
02:30:02,517 --> 02:30:06,156
they force you that I can't spend the rest of my life with them.

2577
02:30:06,236 --> 02:30:06,700
I'm sorry.

2578
02:30:06,780 --> 02:30:10,465
Anyway, I noticed two or three things in your talk.

2579
02:30:10,545 --> 02:30:15,285
First of all, you've done wonderful for yourself, which I'm really, really happy about.

2580
02:30:15,365 --> 02:30:18,972
Now you said that back home when you call, people lack their drive.

2581
02:30:19,052 --> 02:30:20,683
Now I'm not going to deny that.

2582
02:30:20,763 --> 02:30:21,970
Many people lack their drive.

2583
02:30:22,050 --> 02:30:25,250
drive lag and they are happy in the comfort zone.

2584
02:30:25,330 --> 02:30:27,930
But now here comes a technical question.

2585
02:30:28,010 --> 02:30:36,690
Some people keep running all their lives in the race, and then they die.

2586
02:30:36,770 --> 02:30:41,290
Some people say that they don't want to run. I'm okay.

2587
02:30:41,370 --> 02:30:48,870
For example, if a gentleman or a lady is doing a job.

2588
02:30:48,950 --> 02:30:55,806
or a working housewife, children, and they are making a living, they have some savings,

2589
02:30:55,886 --> 02:31:02,376
and they are making a little bit of money every month, they are eating well,

2590
02:31:02,456 --> 02:31:06,670
they are not in debt, there is no problem as such.

2591
02:31:06,750 --> 02:31:10,292
So that bad life is not even that.

2592
02:31:10,372 --> 02:31:14,750
Why have we only made rat racing the parameter?

2593
02:31:16,210 --> 02:31:17,015
look at me, right?

2594
02:31:17,095 --> 02:31:18,047
I am always grinding.

2595
02:31:18,127 --> 02:31:20,093
I am always reinvesting in my equipment.

2596
02:31:20,173 --> 02:31:22,760
I am always doing this, that, traveling, traveling.

2597
02:31:23,720 --> 02:31:29,403
But deep down, I also think that when my child grows up, he will say, brother,

2598
02:31:29,483 --> 02:31:31,783
I don't want these five apartments.

2599
02:31:31,863 --> 02:31:35,330
I wanted you when I was losing my tooth one by one.

2600
02:31:35,410 --> 02:31:37,410
He has broken four teeth, man.

2601
02:31:39,280 --> 02:31:43,040
He's not even, he's going to be five in three weeks, Inshallah.

2602
02:31:43,120 --> 02:31:45,200
So, after five, he breaks.

2603
02:31:45,280 --> 02:31:48,040
But yeah, we'll see what happens.

2604
02:31:48,120 --> 02:31:49,800
So I'm worried about that.

2605
02:31:49,880 --> 02:31:52,200
So yeah, remember that.

2606
02:31:52,280 --> 02:31:54,840
Now see, kids are very young.

2607
02:31:54,920 --> 02:31:56,560
We think that they are young kids.

2608
02:31:56,640 --> 02:31:59,440
When they grow up a little, then I'll spend more time.

2609
02:31:59,520 --> 02:32:00,840
I'll tell you this.

2610
02:32:00,920 --> 02:32:05,640
One of the first initial memories that I have with my father is.

2611
02:32:05,890 --> 02:32:07,810
Now people who know Karachi, let me explain.

2612
02:32:07,890 --> 02:32:11,810
So Kheer House, I don't know if you guys know, is near Amajna Road.

2613
02:32:11,890 --> 02:32:15,810
So I was in that neighborhood, I used to walk from there to Kheer House.

2614
02:32:15,890 --> 02:32:17,810
Across the road there was an Iranian cafe.

2615
02:32:17,890 --> 02:32:21,810
My father would get tea from there and he would get me fruit cake.

2616
02:32:21,890 --> 02:32:24,810
He would get fruit cake for me, he would drink tea himself very quickly.

2617
02:32:24,890 --> 02:32:26,810
And he would buy a piano pen every day.

2618
02:32:26,890 --> 02:32:32,810
He had a lot of pens but he was like, I don't want to help but this one has gone on sale.

2619
02:32:32,890 --> 02:32:33,570
So he would buy a pen every day.

2620
02:32:33,650 --> 02:32:37,250
I don't know why. Maybe he was losing a lot of pens.

2621
02:32:37,330 --> 02:32:42,330
And then from there we would walk towards Dil Pasand Mithai on Amarjana Road.

2622
02:32:42,410 --> 02:32:47,627
Before that, there's a Jamshed, not Jamshed Bagh, I always forget it.

2623
02:32:47,707 --> 02:32:50,170
It's a Montessori, it's a Parsi-run Montessori.

2624
02:32:50,250 --> 02:32:54,890
So I used to go there and there were a lot of kids crying because their parents used to drop them off.

2625
02:32:54,970 --> 02:32:57,530
So I was worried that why were so many kids crying.

2626
02:32:57,610 --> 02:33:00,250
I won't be more than four.

2627
02:33:00,480 --> 02:33:02,800
Exactly Hashim's age, more or less.

2628
02:33:02,880 --> 02:33:05,120
But I still remember that thing.

2629
02:33:05,200 --> 02:33:08,000
I remember those walks with my father.

2630
02:33:08,080 --> 02:33:12,000
So now I think that I'm not doing those walks with Hashim right now.

2631
02:33:12,080 --> 02:33:12,880
Okay?

2632
02:33:12,960 --> 02:33:17,040
So now I'm obviously sitting on the bed and thinking,

2633
02:33:17,120 --> 02:33:20,000
what rhetoric am I doing?

2634
02:33:20,240 --> 02:33:26,639
So if I stay with him, let's say I don't work in Pakistan, I stay with him, UK, Dubai,

2635
02:33:26,719 --> 02:33:27,811
wherever, whatever.

2636
02:33:27,891 --> 02:33:28,350
Okay?

2637
02:33:28,430 --> 02:33:34,350
and I make 4 episodes of a month, 3-4 explainers, I would make enough money to sustain.

2638
02:33:34,430 --> 02:33:39,350
I don't need a big house, I don't need a sports car. I don't need it.

2639
02:33:39,430 --> 02:33:42,350
If it comes, well and good, but I don't need it.

2640
02:33:42,430 --> 02:33:48,350
It doesn't mean I'm lacking the drive, it means that I'm fulfilling, I'm being fulfilled enough.

2641
02:33:48,430 --> 02:33:53,350
So now we have made rat race a measure that yes, this is doing something.

2642
02:33:53,430 --> 02:33:56,100
We are losers, we came at 9 in the morning and came at 5.

2643
02:33:56,180 --> 02:33:58,540
No, that's also a good life. It's not bad.

2644
02:33:58,620 --> 02:34:03,720
Those who want to sell the course will obviously abuse you because they want to sell their course.

2645
02:34:03,800 --> 02:34:09,457
But if a man leaves his children at school in the morning and goes to work,

2646
02:34:09,537 --> 02:34:17,060
his wife is picking up the kids from school and he is coming home in the evening and they are eating together.

2647
02:34:17,140 --> 02:34:20,520
I think it's the best life. That is what life is supposed to be.

2648
02:34:20,600 --> 02:34:23,330
Now we have set our own challenges.

2649
02:34:23,410 --> 02:34:27,155
The set of challenges, actually, you and I, I'm talking about you,

2650
02:34:27,235 --> 02:34:30,530
we have seen so much poverty that we don't want to go back there.

2651
02:34:30,610 --> 02:34:35,410
So we are so traumatized by that neighborhood, that filth, that poverty.

2652
02:34:35,490 --> 02:34:39,450
Dude, poverty is like the worst thing that can ever happen to anyone.

2653
02:34:40,120 --> 02:34:41,057
Oh man, stop it.

2654
02:34:41,137 --> 02:34:44,011
It's 2 o'clock at night, man.

2655
02:34:44,091 --> 02:34:48,320
I swear, if I had acid, I would have thrown acid on their faces.

2656
02:34:48,490 --> 02:34:50,190
The problem is that I am a famous man.

2657
02:34:50,270 --> 02:34:55,190
If I'm a famous person, the case will increase and media will make sure I go to jail.

2658
02:34:55,270 --> 02:34:57,190
If I was an unknown person, I would have paid money and come out.

2659
02:34:57,270 --> 02:35:01,190
Either I shoot them in the head or I throw a gun at them.

2660
02:35:01,270 --> 02:35:05,270
You see, my father is 80 years old and he is sleeping here.

2661
02:35:09,450 --> 02:35:12,030
And there are so many people like this in this world.

2662
02:35:12,330 --> 02:35:16,430
Now people will say, you should change your house. Like that is a solution.

2663
02:35:16,510 --> 02:35:20,110
Man, there are other people too, what about them? I will do it, what about them?

2664
02:35:20,190 --> 02:35:26,030
I'm sorry guys, man, I get detracted after roaming around. Clearly I'm being detracted, right?

2665
02:35:26,110 --> 02:35:29,990
I can't ignore so much noise. And then you have to hear the same things after roaming around.

2666
02:35:30,070 --> 02:35:34,830
I'm strictly against repeating myself. I know I repeat myself a lot.

2667
02:35:34,910 --> 02:35:37,310
So, there's a constant.

2668
02:35:37,390 --> 02:35:38,670
Constant noise.

2669
02:35:39,550 --> 02:35:41,550
Constant noise. Pakistan has a lot of noise.

2670
02:35:41,830 --> 02:35:43,070
Pakistan, India, Bangladesh.

2671
02:35:43,710 --> 02:35:46,310
There is no peace here. People are crazy.

2672
02:35:47,070 --> 02:35:48,310
I swear I feel like.

2673
02:35:48,590 --> 02:35:50,070
You do one thing.

2674
02:35:50,470 --> 02:35:52,030
You are watching the episode on Friday.

2675
02:35:52,430 --> 02:35:53,590
Tomorrow is Saturday.

2676
02:35:54,270 --> 02:35:56,070
Order popcorn, order pizza pizza.

2677
02:35:56,710 --> 02:35:58,670
There is a movie by Michael Douglas called Falling Down.

2678
02:35:58,750 --> 02:36:01,150
You watch that. You will understand where I come from.

2679
02:36:01,230 --> 02:36:02,830
And you will understand where he comes from.

2680
02:36:02,910 --> 02:36:03,870
You watch that movie.

2681
02:36:05,600 --> 02:36:08,880
So a friend of mine told me a long time ago that I will become this.

2682
02:36:08,960 --> 02:36:12,160
Because these things used to bother me always.

2683
02:36:15,600 --> 02:36:20,720
What was I saying? Yes, so we are so traumatized by that poverty, by that life, that we are still scared.

2684
02:36:20,800 --> 02:36:26,880
That we may not go there again. That's why we are working harder than required.

2685
02:36:26,960 --> 02:36:32,160
And we have gone so far by working so hard that we are not even able to see the right person.

2686
02:36:32,480 --> 02:36:33,920
I feel like he's not right.

2687
02:36:34,520 --> 02:36:37,960
Maybe we're not right. We're running in vain.

2688
02:36:38,400 --> 02:36:40,520
I don't know man, it's a subjective thing.

2689
02:36:40,840 --> 02:36:45,800
But I'm starting to think that, man, that life is not bad either.

2690
02:36:45,880 --> 02:36:50,560
If your friend, you think there's no drive, is it only a drive to go out of the country?

2691
02:36:51,120 --> 02:36:53,240
Living in the country can also be a drive, right?

2692
02:36:53,480 --> 02:37:00,080
If his, that's fine, I'm comfortable where I am, that's a good life.

2693
02:37:00,370 --> 02:37:02,850
Why stress? Why tension?

2694
02:37:03,600 --> 02:37:07,181
So this too, we have, you talk about influencers,

2695
02:37:07,261 --> 02:37:11,852
we have put this thing in the hearts of FOMO people, that until this life is not there,

2696
02:37:11,932 --> 02:37:13,229
we are missing something.

2697
02:37:13,309 --> 02:37:16,202
No, man, how can everyone's life be the same?

2698
02:37:16,282 --> 02:37:18,322
So this is a wrong thought.

2699
02:37:18,402 --> 02:37:20,090
You should not think like that.

2700
02:37:20,770 --> 02:37:28,320
Yes, if you think that they are not progressing at all and are being victim of inflation.

2701
02:37:28,400 --> 02:37:31,320
They feel that their salary has increased by 50,000 from last year.

2702
02:37:31,400 --> 02:37:34,400
Inflation has increased by 10%.

2703
02:37:34,860 --> 02:37:39,000
If they are not securing themselves financially, they are irresponsible,

2704
02:37:39,080 --> 02:37:44,179
and you feel that they have a lot of talent and they are not using their talent properly,

2705
02:37:44,259 --> 02:37:48,320
then we can say that yes, they are lacking a little drive.

2706
02:37:48,400 --> 02:37:54,400
But making this measure is also wrong that why are you not coming out? Oh, don't come out.

2707
02:37:55,500 --> 02:37:58,094
I beg my brother to move out.

2708
02:37:58,174 --> 02:37:59,472
I'll fund everything.

2709
02:37:59,552 --> 02:38:04,096
I beg my brother abroad to come back and beg this one to go outside.

2710
02:38:04,176 --> 02:38:05,686
I will fund everything.

2711
02:38:05,766 --> 02:38:12,089
Which shop to open, which store to run, which travel agency to open, I'll do the finance,

2712
02:38:12,169 --> 02:38:12,876
but do that.

2713
02:38:12,956 --> 02:38:14,835
But he's fine.

2714
02:38:14,915 --> 02:38:17,268
He's like, I'm comfortable.

2715
02:38:17,348 --> 02:38:18,318
I don't want it.

2716
02:38:18,398 --> 02:38:19,777
You wouldn't want it.

2717
02:38:19,857 --> 02:38:20,827
I don't want it.

2718
02:38:20,907 --> 02:38:21,900
I'm happy with this.

2719
02:38:21,980 --> 02:38:23,900
I travel once every four years.

2720
02:38:23,980 --> 02:38:27,900
I travel four times a month and I still don't feel like I'm traveling.

2721
02:38:27,980 --> 02:38:31,900
So yeah, some people are okay with where they are. And let them be.

2722
02:38:31,980 --> 02:38:34,900
I have now, with this time, made it a little difficult to judge people.

2723
02:38:34,980 --> 02:38:36,900
So anyway, again, it's a subjective thing.

2724
02:38:36,980 --> 02:38:40,900
Secondly, what you said, I totally agree with you.

2725
02:38:40,980 --> 02:38:44,900
I agree that I have also noticed this when I travel overseas.

2726
02:38:44,980 --> 02:38:49,840
When people meet, especially in America or Western countries, other countries.

2727
02:38:49,920 --> 02:38:50,550
Europe, etc.

2728
02:38:50,630 --> 02:38:51,379
They are full.

2729
02:38:51,459 --> 02:38:53,395
They have a lot to talk about.

2730
02:38:58,963 --> 02:39:01,627
Because they are tired of talking in English.

2731
02:39:01,707 --> 02:39:03,571
It bothers a person.

2732
02:39:03,651 --> 02:39:05,584
See, a person is a natural tribal.

